/P 93 0 R
/E (MacQueen \(1967\) introduced the K-Means clustering algorithm, one of the most widely used unsupervised machine learning techniques for customer segmentation. The algorithm partitions data into clusters by minimizing the distance between data points and cluster centroids. This method became a foundation for many modern clustering applications.)
